# The source model is fetched by tools/make-block-mesh.py rather than committed,
# so the licence stays with its source and the repository carries only what
# Besiege loads. Run the tool and it downloads this again.
tools/models/*.glb

# Build scratch and Python bytecode.
tools/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Besiege's screenshots, which is how a problem gets described in this repo:
# they are dropped in the working copy, looked at, and are of no use afterwards.
# Named by the game as <yyyymmddhhmmss>_<n>.jpg, so a picture that is meant to be
# kept -- docs/something.png -- is not caught by this.
[0-9]*_[0-9].jpg
[0-9]*_[0-9].png
